ion":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98473","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98473","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98473.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98473.patch","merged_at":"2024-10-24T18:29:28Z"},"body":"Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-docs/issues/10132. If this PR is not approved, the original issue should be closed as not planned.\r\n\r\nAdds links to the `@GlobalScope` functions `str()`, `str_to_var()`, and `var_to_str()` from the `String` class ref. These are the only three `@GlobalScope` functions that are clearly related to strings, rather than just using strings incidentally.\r\n\r\nThese three functions are of interest to users looking at the string documentation. These functions could just as easily have been implemented as static functions `String.from()`, `String.to_var()`, and `String.from_var()`. So it's due to implementation choices and the class reference's inflexibility that these functions are not currently shown on the `String` class reference. All that, and the fact that at least one user noticed their absence in the `String` class ref, makes them worth linking.\r\n\r\nI personally don't mind the status quo in which these functions are not linked from the `String` page. One way or another, this PR should close the original issue, as either implemented or not planned.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_